course: dictionary
lesson: 1075
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Bower» is one of them. In a garden, a bower is a shady, pleasant place under trees or climbing plants. In an old poem, a bower can be a private bedroom. In science, a bower is the display a bowerbird makes to attract a female.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. Look at the words around the word. «Male satin bowerbirds build a stick bower and decorate it with blue things such as flowers, feathers and bottle caps» is about birds, so bower means the bird's display, not a garden or a room.
explain: Test your choice. Put your meaning in the sentence in place of the word. If «a stick display» still makes sense in the bird sentence, you have picked the right meaning. If you try «a shady garden» there, it does not fit, so the clue tells you to choose again.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Bower» can mean a shady place under trees or climbing plants.
fact: In old poems, «bower» can mean a private room or bedroom, especially a lady's.
fact: A bowerbird builds a bower and decorates it to attract a female. A bower is not a nest, but a stage to impress.
fact: When a word has several meanings, the other words in the sentence show you which one to use.
exercise: «Male satin bowerbirds build a stick bower and decorate it with blue things.» What is a bower in this sentence? | A shady place for a picnic | A private bedroom in an old castle | *The display a bowerbird makes to attract a female | A type of climbing rose
exercise: In old poems, lovers meet in a rose bower. What is a rose bower? | A bird's nest made of thorns | *A shady, pleasant place under climbing roses | A bedroom with rose-patterned walls
exercise: «Male bowerbirds in Australia build a bower of sticks, which is not a nest.» What is a bower NOT, according to this sentence? | *A nest | A place decorated with blue flowers | A stage to impress females
test: In an old tale, the princess sat in her bower high in the tower, reading by the window. What does bower mean here? | A bunch of blue flowers | The display a bird makes | *A private bedroom | A garden under trees
test: «Decorate it with blue things such as flowers, feathers and bottle caps.» What does decorate tell you about the bower? | It is hidden under the ground | *It has pretty things added to it to be noticed | It is built from stone
exam: A bowerbird builds a bower and fills it with blue bottle tops to impress a female. Which meaning of bower fits? | *The display made by a bowerbird | A private bedroom | A shady place in a garden | A climbing plant
